From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:20:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 094/148] [ae-patch] Check a global policy's factory_params by
 building its factory once, and accept them on PATCH /v1/policies/{id}

The Global Policies page could switch and delete a global policy but not
change its parameters: UpdateDefaultPolicyRequest took only name, handler
and enabled. It now takes factory_params, which replace the stored ones whole
(omitted leaves them, null or {} clears them).

The new omnigent/server/routes/ae_default_policy_params.py checks params the
way the create route does (registry schema) and then builds the factory once,
because the schema covers key names and JSON types only and a stored policy
whose factory raises breaks policy evaluation for every session. The create
route runs the same check, and a PATCH that changes only the handler checks
the stored params against the new one, so neither path can store params the
factory rejects. update_default gains the field behind a sentinel, so callers
that leave it out keep today's behavior. openapi.json regenerated.
